# Terraform working directories (not the lock file - that should be
# committed for reproducible provider versions, per Terraform's own
# recommendation).
**/.terraform/

# State files - state now lives in the S3 backend (see terraform/backend.tf
# and bootstrap/), but keep this excluded in case anyone ever runs Terraform
# without the backend configured.
**/terraform.tfstate
**/terraform.tfstate.backup

# Saved plan files - regenerated by every `terraform plan -out=...`, and can
# contain sensitive values from state. Never useful to commit.
**/tfplan
**/plan
**/plan.txt
*.tfplan

# Crash logs
**/crash.log

# Downloaded local tooling (e.g. the session-manager-plugin .deb) - not
# repo content, just a local install artifact.
*.deb

# Private keys - never commit these
*.pem
*.ppk

# terraform.tfvars is intentionally NOT ignored here: every variable in this
# repo's tfvars (subnet id, allowed CIDR, state bucket/table names) is
# environment config, not a secret. If a genuinely sensitive value is ever
# needed, put it in a separate *.auto.tfvars file and ignore that
# specifically instead of blanket-ignoring all tfvars.
